<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Peklo u České Lípy bledule traverse — Zahrádky station, public castle-side ground, Karba, Peklo gorge and Dubice [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Zahrádky railway station, complete the station approach and the short public red-marked castle-side street spur, returning from the spur the same way. Continue through Karba along the Robečský stream gorge, using its bridges and boardwalks, include the viewpoint spur and finish at Dubice’s Litoměřická road junction. The finish is a road junction, not a transport platform. Allow extra time on this approximately 9.2 km route; height gain and walking time are estimates. Use existing marked pedestrian paths only, with no cycling, private courtyard entry, barriers, flower picking, vegetation damage, fires or unauthorised cave or rock climbing. Carry a current map for the different marking colours. Spring snowflake flowering is weather-dependent and busy; other seasons may still be open. Prefer dry, snow-free daylight and check mud, flooding, wet wood, rock, ice and fallen trees. Follow current local, seasonal and maintenance closures and landowner instructions. A 2025 grazing notice does not establish a current schedule. Check road and station-approach traffic, transport and parking. Postpone if any required station, castle-side, Karba, gorge, viewpoint or Dubice section is unsafe or unavailable; do not replace it with a shorter approach.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Sources: complete captured original OSM map, referenced-node batches and current complete red walking parent. Changes: directed original source edges from 78 complete ways; only duplicate literal shared junction nodes removed. The selected route retains all 313 original positions; canonical display uses the existing source-vertex simplifier. No private planned waypoint or map coordinates, courtyard snaps, synthetic connectors or elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry, not navigation-grade or legal permission. Source map: https://api.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=14.4951806,50.6288329,14.5313634,50.6789692

